00:00:00.860 --> 00:00:04.960
BETH: Speech, language and communication
might all sound the same, but they

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.729
actually have unique meanings.

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:11.550
Speech generally refers to the act of
speaking, and someone with a problem

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:15.540
with speech may have trouble with
hearing or saying specific sounds

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:18.710
or understanding patterns of words.

00:00:18.879 --> 00:00:22.340
Language refers to the ability
to communicate through speech by

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:26.730
delivering and receiving meaningful
messages through reading, or hearing.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:31.850
A child that has problems with language
may not use proper sentence construction

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:36.699
and grammar or may have trouble
deciphering complex sentences or thoughts.

00:00:37.239 --> 00:00:41.470
Communication can be verbal or
non-verbal using body language.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:46.960
It may involve the use of sarcasm,
gestures, or facial expressions which

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:51.399
give an indication of the meaning of what
someone is trying to communicate to them.

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:56.840
Most people learn to communicate from
birth, however, if that development is

00:00:56.840 --> 00:01:01.690
slowed down or interrupted, a child may
not learn about watching and listening to

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:06.570
people when they are talking, the meaning
of words, or how to hold a conversation.

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:11.909
When communication does not develop
as expected it makes it hard to

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:16.179
understand what people are saying,
say what you want or feel, and the

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:18.470
world can seem a very scary place.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:23.420
An individual may then decide to
withdraw into their own little world.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:28.499
Speech and language delays have
many possible causes, but they

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:29.940
are known to accompany Autism.

00:01:30.549 --> 00:01:35.560
In some instances, however, more than
one factor may cause this, for instance,

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:40.740
dyslexia and other learning disabilities
can lead to language delays in some cases

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:43.070
and often this co-exists with Autism.

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:47.479
Children with Autism can
find it hard to relate to and

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:48.860
communicate with other people.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:53.240
They might be slower to develop
language, have no language at all.

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:58.190
They may have significant problems
with understanding or using spoken

00:01:58.190 --> 00:02:02.050
language and are not always able
to use gestures to make up for

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:03.789
the problems they have with words.

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:09.530
In addition to late speech, there are
a number of other communication-related

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:11.340
issues that relate to autism.

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:16.510
In general, children with autism are
more likely to be slow to respond

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:19.930
to their name or other verbal
attempts to gain their attention

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:24.870
They may speak only in single words
or repeat certain phrases over and

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:32.729
over, seeming unable to combine words
into meaningful sentences, or repeat

00:02:32.729 --> 00:02:33.037
words or phrases that they hear.

00:02:33.037 --> 00:02:37.769
They may use words that seem odd, out
of place, or have a special meaning

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:41.420
known only to those familiar with
the child's way of communicating.

00:02:42.119 --> 00:02:46.120
They may also learn to communicate
in different ways like using

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:48.830
pictures or their own sign language.

